  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****  * @return none.
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****  *
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****  * @details
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****  * <b>Scaling and Overflow Behavior:</b>
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****  *
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****  * \par
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****  * The function is implemented using a 32-bit internal accumulator.
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****  * Both the inputs are represented in 1.7 format and multiplications yield a 2.14 result.
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****  * The 2.14 intermediate results are accumulated in a 32-bit accumulator in 18.14 format.
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****  * This approach provides 17 guard bits and there is no risk of overflow as long as <code>max(srcAL
  57:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****  * The 18.14 result is then truncated to 18.7 format by discarding the low 7 bits and saturated to 
  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****  *
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****  * \par
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****  * Refer the function <code>arm_correlate_opt_q7()</code> for a faster implementation of this funct
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****  *
  62:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****  */
