 700:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****   /* The algorithm implementation is based on the lengths of the inputs. */
 701:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****   /* srcB is always made to slide across srcA. */
 702:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****   /* So srcBLen is always considered as shorter or equal to srcALen */
 703:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****   /* But CORR(x, y) is reverse of CORR(y, x) */
 704:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****   /* So, when srcBLen > srcALen, output pointer is made to point to the end of the output buffer */
 705:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****   /* and a varaible, inv is set to 1 */
 706:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****   /* If lengths are not equal then zero pad has to be done to  make the two
 707:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****    * inputs of same length. But to improve the performance, we include zeroes
 708:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****    * in the output instead of zero padding either of the the inputs*/
 709:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****   /* If srcALen > srcBLen, (srcALen - srcBLen) zeroes has to included in the
 710:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****    * starting of the output buffer */
 711:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_correlate_q7.c ****   /* If srcALen < srcBLen, (srcALen - srcBLen) zeroes has to included in the
